---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/Learn/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout title="Astro + GSAP Learn">
  <header class="learn-hero">
    <p class="learn-eyebrow">Learning phase · product films untouched</p>
    <h1>Five sessions. Real pages.</h1>
    <p>
      Open each route in the browser, click the demos, then View Source / DevTools to see what
      Astro baked into HTML vs what GSAP runs after load. This is your temporary classroom at
      <code>/learn/*</code>.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="learn-grid">
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/01-astro-basics">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 01</span>
      <h2>Astro basics</h2>
      <p>Pages → URLs, components, public assets, build-time vs client scripts.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/02-props-slots">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 02</span>
      <h2>Props + slots</h2>
      <p>Pass data into components; nest HTML with default and named slots.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/03-build-assets">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 03</span>
      <h2>Build & assets</h2>
      <p>What <code>astro build</code> emits, public vs src, why Webflow Cloud cares.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/04-gsap-flip">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 04</span>
      <h2>GSAP Flip</h2>
      <p>Animate layout changes — grid ↔ list, thumbnail ↔ feature.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/05-set-piece">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 05</span>
      <h2>Landing set piece</h2>
      <p>ScrambleText + MorphSVG + ScrollTrigger — competition-ready craft.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/06-explore">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 06</span>
      <h2>Explore more</h2>
      <p>DrawSVG + MotionPath + timelines + CustomWiggle + Observer.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/07-kitchen-sink">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 07</span>
      <h2>Kitchen sink</h2>
      <p>Dump of plugins — stagger, Flip, Drag, Physics2D, eases, and more.</p>
    </a>
    <a class="learn-card" href="/learn/08-gsdevtools">
      <span class="learn-card__n">Session 08</span>
      <h2>GSDevTools</h2>
      <p>The YouTube scrubber UI — play, pause, loop, in/out on a real timeline.</p>
    </a>
  </div>

  <div class="learn-callout" style="margin-top: 2rem">
    <strong>How to use this:</strong> do sessions in order. On each page, do the “Try this”
    checklist before moving on. Ask questions on anything that feels fuzzy — we’ll go deeper
    on that route.
  </div>
</LearnLayout>
